#AUTO 38
#NEEDED 1
# Audio-codec recon (issue 110n) — TEMPORARY, probe-and-remove.
#
# The RK817 PMIC integrates the audio codec, reachable over i2c0 (which is up).
# We don't have the RK817 datasheet yet to name the codec registers, so this
# dumps the chip's whole i2c register space (0x00-0xFF) to capture the raw
# codec state — recon-ahead for the audio path, no I2S bring-up needed.
#
# This is a one-board OS: once the board's audio-codec registers are recorded
# in the audio issue file, this probe has done its job — run it once, save the
# dump, then REMOVE it (probe-and-remove). Read-only over i2c.

CALL audio_recon
